course: dictionary
lesson: 13606
title: Incubation: keeping things warm and growing
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Incubation is a word for a period of waiting while something grows and develops in the right conditions. Eggs need warmth for incubation, and new ideas, like a plant or a business, can need time and care to grow. «The eggs stayed warm in the incubator during incubation.» The eggs are not hatching yet. They are being kept warm so they can develop.
explain: In health, incubation means the time between catching an illness and feeling the first signs of it. «The incubation period for chickenpox is about two weeks.» So a child can spread chickenpox for days before they feel ill. The illness is growing inside the body during that time, even though nothing looks wrong.
explain: Check the sense with the clues around the word. Is it about eggs, illness, or growing? If the sentence talks about warmth, eggs, or waiting for something to develop, incubation probably means the careful waiting that helps something grow. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Incubation means keeping something in the right conditions so it can develop.
fact: «Incubation» is often used with eggs: a chicken egg takes about 21 days of incubation to hatch.
fact: In medicine, the «incubation period» is the time between catching an illness and showing the first signs.
fact: «Incubation» can also mean keeping an idea, a bacteria culture, or a new business in the right conditions so it can grow.
exercise: «The chicks were ready to hatch after the incubation of the eggs.» What does incubation mean here? | *Keeping eggs warm so they can develop | Breaking eggs into a bowl | Cooking eggs for breakfast | Counting eggs in a box
exercise: «The incubation period for chickenpox is about two weeks.» What is an incubation period? | Time spent in bed with a fever | *Time between catching an illness and showing the first signs | Time when you feel completely well | Time to wait for a vaccine
exercise: «The new club idea needed careful incubation before it could grow.» What does incubation mean here? | Writing the idea down in a letter | Telling everyone about the idea at once | Throwing the idea away | *Keeping the idea in the right conditions so it can grow
test: How long is the incubation of a chicken egg? | About 21 years | About 21 minutes | About 21 days | *About 21 days, but this is for chickens and can vary
test: Which phrase means the time before an illness shows its first signs? | egg shell | incubation of eggs | *incubation period | incubator
exam: Ella says incubation means cracking eggs open for breakfast. What does incubation really mean? | Cooking eggs in hot water | *Keeping eggs warm so they can develop and hatch | Counting eggs in a box | Cracking eggs open
